    "title": "What stores are open and closed on Easter Sunday 2026?",
    "text": "April 2, 2026, 5:21 a.m. ETEaster Sunday falls on April 5 this year, marking one of the most important holidays in the Christian faith — the celebration of Jesus Christ’s resurrection. As a result, many stores and restaurants will be closed in observance.Here's what to expect if you're heading out to shop on the holiday.What stores are closed on Easter this year?The following stores are among those that will be closed on Sunday, April 5:TargetCostcoSam's ClubLowe'sTJ Maxx, Marshalls, and HomeGoodsMacy'sAldiAppleNordstrom and Nordstrom RackJCPenneyKohl'sBurlingtonOffice Depot and OfficeMaxMichaelsHobby LobbyDick's Sporting GoodsWhat stores are open on Easter this year?These stores will be open, though some may have reduced hours:Walmart – Open regular hoursWegmans - Open regular hours, some departments have reduced hoursHome Depot – Open 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.CVS Pharmacy - Open. Hours vary by locationIKEA – Open 11 a.m. to 6 p.m.Tractor Supply Co. – Open 9 a.m. to 6 p.m.Why does Easter change every year?Easter does not have a fixed date. In Western Christianity, it is celebrated on the first Sunday after the first full moon following the spring equinox (March 21). Because of this, Easter can fall anywhere between March 22 and April 25. Eastern Orthodox churches calculate the date using the Julian calendar, which is why their Easter is often observed later.Key Easter-related dates in 2026Palm Sunday: March 29Holy Thursday (Maundy Thursday): April 2Good Friday: April 3Easter Sunday: April 5What is Easter?Easter is one of the most important holidays in Christianity, celebrating the resurrection of Jesus Christ. It marks the culmination of Holy Week, which includes Palm Sunday, Holy Thursday and Good Friday.",
